I sit on the sofa and take my phone in my hand.
I open the electricity board's website.
Usually, I avoid such boring tasks.
But today I have to update my account details.
I go to the profile section.
There are some instructions on the screen.
The language of the website is very formal.
I read the first instruction carefully.
It says, "User information is updated here."
I read the next instruction.
"A new form is submitted from here."
This official language feels a bit difficult to read.
We usually work in simple language at the office.
Here, every sentence is written in such an official manner.
I read the last instruction.
"A code is sent to your mobile number."
I understand the entire process now.
I click on the next page now.
